description:
Use this when the diver asks how long they can stay at a depth without decompression stops (no-deco limit, NDL, no-stop time). Returns the minutes left after the descent at GF high, the PPO₂ of the gas there and its MOD at 1.4 bar, a safety-stop reminder and a Dive Kit share link. Suits beginners and recreational divers. Not for a full dive plan (plan_dive) or a gas-limited bottom time (find_max_bottom_time).

Computed by the Dive Kit app's Bühlmann ZH-L16C engine; agency tables and dive computers differ. Default gas air, GF 50/80. For "is 25 min at 30 m ok?" send bottom_time_min: the answer says within or over, and by how much. For a repetitive dive pass the previous result's share link and the surface interval.

Example: {"depth":18}
